WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.710
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:03.840
it.

3
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:09.170
Just follow along step by step. Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12

4
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:09.920
tablets each

5
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.680
and a measured container. Start your first dose between 6 and 7 p.m. the night

6
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:16.720
before your procedure.

7
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:22.050
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets. Fill the provided container with 16

8
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:22.640
ounces of

9
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.170
water up to the fill line. Swallow one tablet every two minutes with a sip of

10
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:27.840
water,

11
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.750
finishing all 12 tablets over about 15 to 20 minutes. Take your time and go at

12
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:33.760
a steady pace.

13
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.560
About one hour after your last tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces

14
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:39.200
of water

15
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.950
and drink the entire amount slowly over 30 minutes. Then, about 30 minutes

16
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:44.640
after finishing

17
00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.140
that container, fill it one more time with 16 ounces of water and drink the

18
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:49.600
entire amount

19
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:55.330
over 30 minutes. That completes your first dose. Repeat the exact same three

20
00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:56.800
steps using your second

21
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.380
bottle of 12 tablets. One tablet every two minutes with water, then 16 ounces

22
00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:02.640
of water one hour later,

23
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.390
then 16 ounces of water, 30 minutes after that. This part is really important.

24
00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:08.000
You must drink

25
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.350
all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already passing clear

26
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:11.920
liquid.

27
00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.320
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

28
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:16.720
the clearest

29
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.560
view during your procedure. If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may

30
00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:21.760
need to reschedule,

31
00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.100
and neither of us wants that. Between doses, keep drinking clear liquids to

32
00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:26.880
stay hydrated.

33
00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.670
It will help you feel better and help the prep do its job. Do not drink

34
00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:32.320
anything at all within

35
00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.460
four hours of your procedure, including water, unless it is a small sip to take

36
00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:37.360
a medication.

37
00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:42.110
Your procedure may be canceled or rescheduled if this is not followed. If you

38
00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:43.200
experience any

39
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.680
discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying a petroleum-based

40
00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:48.480
ointment or diaper rash

41
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:54.560
cream can really help. That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish

42
00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.360
the full dose,

43
00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.860
and stay hydrated. If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our

44
00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:02.560
office. We're here to help.
